description:
From slice-8 review: public API now has four run entries — run, run_with_width, run_with_segments, run_with_segments_and_width. Cross-product will grow as themes, tool-filtering, tick-mode, etc. land.

Consider a builder before 0.1 locks SemVer:

    pub struct Runner<'a> { /* segments, width, theme, ... */ }
    impl<'a> Runner<'a> {
        pub fn new() -> Self;
        pub fn segments(self, segments: &'a [Box<dyn Segment>]) -> Self;
        pub fn terminal_width(self, w: u16) -> Self;
        pub fn run(self, r: impl Read, w: impl Write) -> io::Result<()>;
    }

Or at minimum pass an Options struct. Decide before 0.1.0 tag.
